WEBVTT

00:00:05.267 --> 00:00:07.067
Until now, the microphone in the

00:00:07.067 --> 00:00:09.433
TypeWhisper keyboard opened the app first.

00:00:10.067 --> 00:00:12.133
Then you had to find your way back.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:17.633
With version 1.3, the keyboard records by itself.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.633
“I'm on my way, be there in ten minutes.”

00:00:22.933 --> 00:00:26.167
The text lands in your message, and you never left the chat.

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:30.600
“Coffee is on me.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:31.833
Thumbs up emoji.”

00:00:33.367 --> 00:00:35.633
The next sentence starts with a space,

00:00:35.633 --> 00:00:37.400
and you can say emoji by name.

00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:42.067
With Premium, Record in the Keyboard is on from the start.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.667
You can turn it off under Settings, Keyboard.

00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:49.533
On an iPhone 17, Fast Local recognizes

00:00:49.533 --> 00:00:52.400
a short dictation in about 0.3 seconds.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.333
It works with Apple Speech, Fast Local,

00:00:55.333 --> 00:00:58.600
Fluid Speech Pro and cloud services with your own key.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:02.500
Open TypeWhisper later, and every dictation is in your History.

00:01:03.733 --> 00:01:06.133
Good to know: music pauses while you dictate,

00:01:06.133 --> 00:01:08.933
and your dictionary and snippets apply here as well.

00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:11.333
Record in the Keyboard.

00:01:11.333 --> 00:01:13.100
New in TypeWhisper 1.3.

00:01:13.733 --> 00:01:16.167
Get TypeWhisper free on the App Store.
